    "body": "Scope addition from the second read of PR #3472: PR #3472 reads the chuck side of a part-off as -Z (ISO 841). No setup or machine field states which spindle holds the bar. This parameter (or a setup field) must also carry the chuck side, so that a part held from the +Z side (a sub-spindle, or a mirrored setup) can be parted. Until then, #3472 refuses a plane that has the whole model on the -Z side of it.",
