    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T15:20:56Z",
    "body": "Labels changed: `enhancement` / `P6` to `bug` / `P3`. Reason: the fix of #3452 (PR #3472) must refuse a part-off in a flipped second setup, because the code cannot know which side of the plane is the finished part. In that setup the part is held in the chuck and a stub is cut off the free end (second read of PR #3472, comment 7081220126). A legal program is then refused until the user can state the side. That is the `P3` class of the priority table.\n\nScope of this issue after that fact: one parameter with a default, \"The part is: the piece that is cut off (default) / the piece that stays in the chuck\", through the command, the project key, the MCP tool and the Passes or Geometry row. The kerf goes fully on the other side. The refusal for a flipped setup goes away when the parameter exists. The allowance on the back face stays in the scope.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
