    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T15:47:37Z",
    "body": "Fact from the third read of PR #3472: a part-off with the parting plane inside the model is now refused by name in two cases. (1) An aligned setup that does not hold the part as modelled, for example the OP20 flip. (2) A setup with a part that is modelled lying down (along X or Y), because no setup is as modelled for it. This parameter is the way back for both cases. A part-off with the plane at an end of the model still generates in each setup.",
